      "13/02/2026 15:01  \n\nPartner 😄  \nLet’s reduce confusion → convert into **clear food flow** for today + weekend.\n\nYou already had **wheat dosa** in the morning ✅  \nNow fridge has **vaazhaipoo (banana flower)**  \nAlso have **roasted semiya**\n\nLet’s structure this calmly.\n\n---\n\n## 🌾 1️⃣ Wheat Dosa (Morning – Done)\nimage_group{\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"wheat dosa on tawa\",\"godhuma dosa south indian\",\"wheat dosa crispy edges\",\"wheat dosa with chutney\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\n\nLight, simple, already eaten.  \nSo evening should not repeat heavy wheat again.\n\n---\n\n## 🌸 2️⃣ Vaazhaipoo Rice (Best for Tonight or Tomorrow Lunch)\nimage_group{\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"vaazhaipoo cleaning process\",\"banana flower chopped\",\"vaazhaipoo poriyal\",\"vaazhaipoo rice south indian\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\n\nIf vaazhaipoo is already in fridge → don’t delay too long.  \nIt darkens and slightly turns bitter if kept.\n\n### Smart Plan:\n- Clean & chop now (20 min)\n- Cook simple **vaazhaipoo poriyal**\n- Mix with hot rice + ghee → done\n\nWhy today?\nBecause it’s fibrous + nutritious.  \nWeekend cooking becomes relaxed after that.\n\n---\n\n## 🍜 3️⃣ Samiya Upma (Weekend Morning Special)\nimage_group{\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"roasted semiya upma\",\"vermicelli upma south indian\",\"lemon semiya upma\",\"ghee semiya upma\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\n\nPerfect for:\n- Saturday breakfast  \n- Light dinner  \n- Or lazy Sunday\n\nFast, flexible, less prep stress.\n\n---\n\n# 🧭 Decision Matrix (No Overthinking)\n\n| Time | What to Eat | Why |\n|------|-------------|------|\n| Evening Today | Vaazhaipoo Rice | Use fresh ingredient |\n| Weekend Morning | Samiya Upma | Quick & light |\n| Weekend Night | Leftover / simple curd rice | Digestive reset |\n\n---\n\n# 🧠 Energy Logic\n\nYou said:\n> sleep eat if possible work\n\nSo we choose:\n- Today = nutritious but not heavy\n- Weekend = variety but simple\n- No repeated wheat overload\n\n---\n\n# Final Clear Suggestion\n\n👉 **Today evening → Vaazhaipoo rice**  \n👉 **Saturday morning → Lemon ghee semiya upma**  \n👉 Night → keep simple\n\nConfusion removed.  \nNo food waste.  \nNo heavy stomach.  \nWeekend balanced.\n\nIf you want, I’ll give:\n- 15-minute ultra-fast vaazhaipoo version  \nOR  \n- Rich temple-style version  \n\nTell me which mode today:  \n⚡ Fast  \nor  \n🌿 Traditional slow calm cooking?"
